* Behavioural models for the flight controller's circuit simulations. Each is written from the
* part type's published behaviour (reference, switching frequency, drive strength), not from a
* vendor netlist.

* 36 V 2 A synchronous buck, 500 kHz, 0.8 V reference, 1 ms internal soft start, voltage mode
* with input feedforward and an internal type-II compensator. Under-voltage lockout at 4.5 V:
* until VIN and EN are up, the low-side switch holds SW at ground and COMP is held at 0 V (no
* windup from a load on a dead output); COMP clamps at 2.4 V. Pins: VIN EN BST SW FB GND.
.subckt BUCK36V vin en bst sw fb gnd
Bok ok gnd V = {0.5*(1+tanh((V(vin,gnd)-4.5)*10))*0.5*(1+tanh((V(en,gnd)-1.2)*20))}
Bref ref gnd V = {0.8*min(1, time/1m)*V(ok,gnd)}
Gea gnd comp VALUE = {300u*(V(ref,gnd)-V(fb,gnd))*V(ok,gnd)}
Gdis comp gnd VALUE = {10m*V(comp,gnd)*(1-V(ok,gnd))}
Rea comp gnd 5Meg
Dclh comp clh DCLAMP
Vclh clh gnd 2.4
Dcll ncl comp DCLAMP
Vcll ncl gnd -0.2
.model DCLAMP D(is=1e-12 n=0.05)
Rc comp cz 22k
Cc cz gnd 4.7n
Cp comp gnd 47p
Vramp ramp gnd PULSE(0 1 0 1.96u 20n 20n 2u)
Bpwm ctl gnd V = {V(ok,gnd)*0.5*(1+tanh((limit(V(comp,gnd)*10/max(V(vin,gnd),5), 0, 0.95) - V(ramp,gnd))*60))}
Bctlb ctlb gnd V = {1 - V(ctl,gnd)}
S1 vin sw ctl gnd SWHS
S2 sw gnd ctlb gnd SWLS
.model SWHS SW(vt=0.5 vh=0 ron=0.09 roff=10Meg)
.model SWLS SW(vt=0.5 vh=0 ron=0.05 roff=10Meg)
Rbst bst sw 1Meg
Ren en gnd 10Meg
Rfb fb gnd 100Meg
.ends BUCK36V

* The same buck averaged over a switching period: its error amplifier holds FB at the 0.8 V
* reference, so the operating point gives the set output voltage. Pins as BUCK36V.
.subckt BUCK36V_AVG vin en bst sw fb gnd
Eout sw gnd VALUE = {limit(2e4*(0.8 - V(fb,gnd)), 0, V(vin,gnd))}
Rbst bst sw 1Meg
Ren en gnd 10Meg
Rfb fb gnd 100Meg
.ends BUCK36V_AVG

* 3.3 V 300 mA LDO, 250 mV dropout. Pins: VIN EN VOUT GND.
.subckt LDO33 vin en vout gnd
Bldo vout gnd V = {min(3.3, max(V(vin,gnd)-0.25, 0))*0.5*(1+tanh((V(en,gnd)-1)*20))}
Rq vin gnd 50k
Ren en gnd 10Meg
.ends LDO33
